    "intro_narrative": "You awaken in the belly of the Chronos Spire, a legendary steam-powered citadel built by the mad inventor Archimedes Locke. The air is thick with the smell of ozone, hot copper, and machine oil. Surrounding you is a dizzying array of brass calculation engines, hissing pneumatic tubes, and intricate gearwork mechanisms. Your goal is simple but daunting: you must find a way to unlock The Grand Vault hidden somewhere in this mechanical labyrinth. Rumor has it that Locke secured his ultimate blueprint within it, protected by an interlocking web of computational devices and logic engines. To succeed, you will need to decipher the dependencies of these steampunk contraptions, feeding the output of one machine into the next. The boiler pressure is rising, and time is ticking. Explore the room, trace the pneumatic lines, and master the machinery before the Spire undergoes its automated purge cycle.",
    "narrative_style": "steampunk"
  },
